# GraphQL diet (2026-11-01: the daemons on huge-blue and cosmic-gray spent 938 and 833 GraphQL queries an hour, the
# account's biggest spenders, while their clients read about two dozen PRs). A watch nobody has read lately is
# polled about as often as it was last read, a comment wait on a repository the controller's webhooks cover
# relies on them and polls GitHub only as a safety net, and a running head the controller covers is re-read on
# its own check events, so the TTL is only the safety net there too.
IDLE_BACKOFF_AFTER = 300  # a PR nobody has read or waited on for this long is polled as often as it was last read
IDLE_BACKOFF_MAX = 600  # ... but no less often than this (it expires at IDLE_EXPIRY)
# A waited, unfinished watch is read every cycle (60 s; 240 s when lean). Data older than this on one is starved, not
# paced: daemon.json's staleWaited says so, `restart` restarts a daemon whose heartbeat is fresh but whose waited data
# is this old, and a wait hands itself back from the daemon and reads GitHub once itself (direct_read). The heartbeat
