# GitHub's secondary limit is one per account across REST and GraphQL, so a secondary 403 holds both
# buckets (moving the reads to the other one is the burst it asks us not to send), for its Retry-After
# or SECONDARY_BACKOFF doubling with each hit in a row up to SECONDARY_BACKOFF_MAX, whichever is longer.
